    "description": "Remove Direct and Strategic as values from the Partner Type picklist on Partner.\n\n## Why\n\n* Direct only makes sense during Operator deal setup. It is not a standalone Partner attribute. It belongs with the Operator or deal configuration flow, not the Partner record.\n\n* Strategic is already covered by the existing partner flow and referral setup. The label is no longer needed.\n\n## Implementation Requirements\n\n* Remove Direct and Strategic from the Partner Type picklist.\n\n* Check existing Partner records for either value before removal.\n\n* Decide how to reassign any record that currently uses Direct or Strategic.\n\n## Open Questions\n\n* Confirm no automation or report filter references Direct or Strategic on Partner Type.\n\n* Confirm the replacement value for existing records set to Direct or Strategic.\n\n## Source\n\nEmily Vandenberg, Wagertech feedback — Operator & Partner Record Pages doc, WAGERTECH Feedback PARTNER section: \"Partner Type field — remove 'Direct' and 'Strategic' options\" and \"Ask: Remove both values from the Partner Type picklist.\"",
